---
/**
 * Partners (/partners) — Consultancy. Built against the committed Figma node 7385:5219
 * (design/figma/fTqnnV20l9htP7vFJrOsvn/7385-5219/), see docs/consultancy-build-plan.md.
 * Last of the 5 build-plan pages.
 *
 * Not linked from the shared header/footer nav (`src/lib/nav.ts`) — same finding as Team
 * (Phase 4) and Home's original Phase 1 note: confirmed again against this page's own
 * node.json (the shell nodes carry the identical nav, still no `/partners` entry). Built as a
 * valid, tested, but intentionally unlinked route, per the build plan's instruction.
 *
 * Typography confirmed against node.json (not guessed):
 *   - Hero "Strategic Partners": 64/56/700/-0.26 (`--font-size-hero` + `--line-height-h2`/
 *     `--letter-spacing-h2`) — the same one-off composition every other page's hero title uses.
 *     Same shared lecture-hall photo + 25% scrim, bottom-anchored/centred, reused verbatim.
 *   - The lead sentence above the grid ("Together, GIEVA…") is 40/~46/700/0 — matches `.u-h3`
 *     (40/48/700/0) closely enough that the ~2px line-height delta is Figma's intrinsic
 *     auto-line-height, not a bound variable (no `boundVariables.lineHeight` on this node,
 *     unlike every genuinely-token-bound text style elsewhere) — reusing `.u-h3` per the
 *     established "line-height rounds to the nearest role" precedent. Its colour is
 *     `--color-violet` (`#120633`) directly: a genuinely new usage of that primitive as
 *     *text* on a *light* surface — previously only used as a dark-surface background. Not a
 *     new token; the primitive already existed (TOKENS.md primitives are shared across roles).
 *   - Each of the 24 partner-card names is 18/24/700/0 — bold, zero tracking, a combination no
 *     existing named role captures (`.u-body-lg` is 400 weight/-0.16 tracking). Composed
 *     directly from existing primitives (`--font-size-underline`, `--line-height-underline`,
 *     `--letter-spacing-none`, `--font-weight-bold`) in this page's own `<style>` block — same
 *     one-off-composition precedent as Services'/About's/Team's page-local combinations, no new
 *     token added. Card descriptions match `.u-body-lg` (18/24/400/-0.16) exactly — reused as-is.
 *   - "Become a Partner" is `.u-section-title` (48/56/700/-3.3) — confirmed as the *other* named
 *     48px pattern (not `.u-h2`), matching Home's/Services' recurring-headline usage rather than
 *     About's `.u-h2` finding. "Partner" is a bold-italic accent-warm run (confirmed via
 *     `characterStyleOverrides`, override index 4) — the same hook-sentence pattern as every
 *     other page, rendered with the existing `.u-accent-em` utility, no new class needed.
 *   - Form field labels are `.u-body-lg` metrics but `--color-accent-warm`, not the inherited
 *     inverse text colour — composed with an explicit colour override, same technique as the
 *     CTA banner's `.u-eyebrow`/heading colour overrides elsewhere.
 *
 * Content notes confirmed via node.json (not guessed):
 *   - The 24-card grid is Figma's `GRID` auto-layout mode with **manual** item positioning:
 *     document order is NOT visual order (see `partners-content.ts`'s header comment —
 *     "CoLab Innovation Hub" is the one card out of place). Built from a (row, col)-sorted
 *     list so the DOM/reading order matches what's actually seen, not raw document order.
 *   - `gridColumnGap`/`gridRowGap` are both exactly 84px — a genuine new spacing value (not in
 *     the existing 4/8/12/16/24/32/40/48/64/80/96/120 scale) confirmed by (1312 - 3×84) / 4 =
 *     265px matching every card's own bounding-box width exactly. Composed as a page-local
 *     value rather than added to the global scale — see the note above `.partners-grid` below,
 *     same "one-off values don't need a global token" precedent as every prior phase.
 *   - Sterling Bank's card logo (node 8000:9930) has no raster fill AND no named-SVG vector —
 *     every one of its ~40 paths is generically named "Vector", which the fetch helper's
 *     dedup-by-name treats as noise (Phase 0 decision) and skips. Backfilled via a direct
 *     one-node Figma images API render (see `partners-images.ts` + `assets/manifest.json`'s
 *     `notes`) rather than guessing a substitute logo or re-running the whole page's ingestion.
 *   - Datadotorg's description underlines "Data.Org" (confirmed via `characterStyleOverrides`,
 *     `textDecoration: UNDERLINE`) — rendered with the existing `.u-underline` utility.
 *   - Care4Water's description has literal authored line breaks (not organic wrap) — rendered
 *     with `white-space: pre-line` so they're honoured exactly as authored.
 *   - Genuine spelling errors in the source ("paartner", "pandenic", "interract" on the
 *     EDIFACE card) reproduced verbatim per exact-replica-first, same precedent as About's
 *     "Mision".
 *   - No CTA banner on this page — unlike every other page (Home/Services/About/Team), which
 *     all repeat the identical "Ready to Take Your First Step?" block, Partners' own node.json
 *     has no such section: the "Become a Partner" interview form is the page's only closing
 *     block. Confirmed by walking the tree, not assumed from precedent.
 *   - The "Become a Partner" form (node 8000:10047) is a real 7-field `<form>` (name, company
 *     name, company website, industry, phone, email, message) with an explicit `<label>` per
 *     field in the source, right-aligned in a shared column ahead of the input — same
 *     progressively-enhanceable, no-`action`-yet precedent as `SiteFooter`'s newsletter form
 *     (there's no submission endpoint in scope for this build). Implemented as a single CSS
 *     grid (`max-content 1fr` columns) rather than 7 independent flex rows so every label
 *     shares one column width exactly like the source (all input columns start at the same x
 *     regardless of their own label's length) — reproducing the effect without hand-tuning a
 *     fixed pixel column width.
 *
 * Component reuse considered: `ServiceDetailSection` (the ★ template) shapes a
 * title+subtitle/about-covers-cost block; Partners' content (a 24-item logo/name/description
 * directory + a contact form) isn't that shape, so this page writes its own markup, same call
 * as About's and Team's.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { partnersHeroPhoto } from '@lib/partners-images';
import { partnerOrgs, partnerFormFields } from '@lib/partners-content';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Strategic Partners — GIEVA Consultancy"
  description="The organisations, institutions, and companies GIEVA partners with to build a world of opportunities."
  brand="consultancy"
>
  <!-- ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="partners-hero">
    <div class="partners-hero__media">
      <Image
        src={partnersHeroPhoto}
        alt=""
        width={1440}
        height={670}
        class="partners-hero__photo"
      />
      <div class="partners-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container partners-hero__content">
      <h1 class="partners-hero__heading">Strategic Partners</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Partner directory ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section partners-directory">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="u-h3 partners-lead">
        Together, GIEVA and our partners help build a world of opportunities.
      </h2>

      <ul role="list" class="partners-grid">
        {
          partnerOrgs.map((org) => (
            <li class="partner-card">
              <div class="partner-card__logo">
                <Image src={org.logo} alt="" class="partner-card__logo-img" />
              </div>
              <h3 class="partner-card__name">{org.name}</h3>
              <p class="u-body-lg partner-card__desc">
                {org.descriptionUnderline
                  ? org.description.split(org.descriptionUnderline).map((chunk, i, arr) => (
                      <>
                        {chunk}
                        {i < arr.length - 1 && (
                          <span class="u-underline">{org.descriptionUnderline}</span>
                        )}
                      </>
                    ))
                  : org.description}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Become a Partner ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section partners-cta-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="partners-form surface-inverse" data-surface="inverse">
        <div class="partners-form__header">
          <h2 class="u-section-title">
            Become a <em class="u-accent-em">Partner</em>
          </h2>
          <p class="u-body-lg">
            Answer Interview questions to help us know how we can impact lives together
          </p>
        </div>

        <form class="partners-form__fields">
          {
            partnerFormFields.map((field) => (
              <>
                <label class="partners-form__label u-body-lg" for={field.id}>
                  {field.label}
                </label>
                <div class="partners-form__control">
                  <input
                    id={field.id}
                    class="partners-form__input u-body-lg"
                    type={field.type}
                    name={field.id}
                    placeholder="Your Answer"
                    autocomplete={field.autocomplete}
                    required
                  />
                </div>
              </>
            ))
          }
          <div class="partners-form__submit">
            <Button variant="primary" type="submit">Send Message</Button>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Shared section rhythm (matches Home/Services/About/Team) ────────────── */
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--section-padding-block);
  }

  /* ── Hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .partners-hero {
    position: relative;
  }
  .partners-hero__media {
    position: relative;
  }
  .partners-hero__photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .partners-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25);
  }
  .partners-hero__content {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6xl);
  }
  .partners-hero__heading {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-white);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: var(--font-size-hero);
    line-height: var(--line-height-h2);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-h2);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    text-align: center;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* ── Partner directory ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `.partners-lead`'s colour is `--color-violet` directly — see header comment: a genuinely
     new (light-surface text) usage of an existing dark-surface-background primitive. */
  .partners-lead {
    color: var(--color-violet);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* 84px column/row gap is confirmed from node.json's gridColumnGap/gridRowGap (both 84) and
     isn't a step in the shared spacing scale — see header comment for the math. Composed here
     rather than added as a new global token, same precedent as every prior page's one-offs. */
  .partners-grid {
    margin-top: var(--space-4xl);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 84px;
  }
  /* Rows are a roughly uniform ~525-552px in the source regardless of content length (confirmed
     against frame.png — even Care4Water's 7-line paragraph sits in the same row budget as
     "College Board"'s 2-line one, with generous trailing whitespace below shorter cards) —
     an intentional airy rhythm, not organic content-hugging. `min-height` reproduces that
     rhythm while still letting a card whose real content needs more room grow past it, same
     as the source's own row3 (552px) being slightly taller than the rest (525/470). */
  .partner-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-height: 520px;
  }
  .partner-card__logo {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 180px;
  }
  .partner-card__logo-img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  /* The 5px accent-warm top border is a real divider between the logo and the name
     (node.json: `individualStrokeWeights.top: 5` on the heading's own frame, paired with its
     `paddingTop: 24` — border and gap live on the same element in the source). */
  .partner-card__name {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 5px solid var(--color-accent-warm);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: var(--font-size-underline);
    line-height: var(--line-height-underline);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-none);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text-default);
  }
  .partner-card__desc {
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-line;
  }

  /* ── Become a Partner ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Flat dark panel (no corner radius in the source — confirmed, unlike the CTA banner cards
     on every other page, which do use `--radius-md`). */
  .partners-form {
    padding: var(--space-3xl);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .partners-form__header {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    justify-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* 122px column gap confirmed from node.json's itemSpacing on every field row (8000:10056 and
     siblings) — another one-off value outside the shared scale, same precedent as the grid's
     84px above. */
  .partners-form__fields {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    column-gap: 122px;
    row-gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .partners-form__label {
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--color-accent-warm);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .partners-form__control {
    display: flex;
  }
  .partners-form__input {
    width: 100%;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-white);
    padding-block: var(--space-2xs);
    color: var(--color-text-inverse);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
  }
  .partners-form__input::placeholder {
    color: var(--color-text-inverse);
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .partners-form__input:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--color-accent-bright);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .partners-form__submit {
    grid-column: 2;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .partners-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .partners-hero__heading {
      font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
    }
    .partners-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .partners-form__fields {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .partners-form__label {
      text-align: left;
      white-space: normal;
    }
    .partners-form__submit {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
